      "name": "t:sections.n_mi-faq-page-hero-qa.name",
      "settings": {
        "use_own_file": false,
        "heading": "<h1><strong>Her Husband Hadn't Mentioned </strong><em><strong>How Good Her Skin Looked</strong></em><strong> In 26 Years. Then One Tuesday, He Did...</strong> </h1>",
        "text": "<p>Created In Partnership With <strong>Qure Editorial Team</strong></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/MI_-_Stamping_Posing_image_-_apply_2.webp",
        "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/MI_-_Stamping_Posing_image_-_apply_2.webp"
      }
    },
    "n_mi_faq_page_qa_NTk4id": {
      "type": "n_mi-faq-page-qa",
      "name": "t:sections.n_mi-faq-page-qa.name",
      "settings": {
        "use_own_file": false,
        "modifier": "none",
        "updated_info": false,
        "heading": "<p><strong>Rita is 51. </strong></p>",
        "text": "<p>The lines from her nose to the corners of her mouth had been settling in for a few years now. Her skin looked tired even on the days she wasn't. </p><p>She had the full routine. Cleanser, vitamin C, retinol, two moisturisers, SPF. Nothing was working the way it used to.<br/>She tried something that worked on a completely different principle. </p><p>Three treatments later, her husband commented on her skin for the first time in twenty-six years.</p><p>This is what she found. And five skincare habits it's about to retire.</p>"
      }
    },
    "n_mi_faq_page_qa_img_mobile_HpGN7A": {
      "type": "n_mi-faq-page-qa-img-mobile",
      "name": "t:sections.n_mi-faq-page-qa-img-mobile.name",
      "settings": {
        "use_own_file": false,
        "modifier": "img-to-top",
        "heading": "<h2><strong>01. Sorry, the expensive routine wasn't getting anywhere. </strong></h2>",
        "text": "<p>You gave each one the full eight weeks. You followed the layering order. </p><p>You switched the retinol. You upgraded the vitamin C. You spent more than you'd admit on a peptide cream that felt nice for an hour.</p><p>Your skin looked roughly the same. </p><p>The lines settled in anyway. Foundation started catching where it never used to.<br/>The products weren't bad. You weren't doing it wrong. </p><p><strong>They just weren't getting where they needed to go…</strong></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Qure_main-copy_7.webp",
        "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/Qure_main-copy_7.webp"
      }
    },
    "n_mi_faq_page_qa_ykbALR": {
      "type": "n_mi-faq-page-qa",
      "disabled": true,
      "name": "t:sections.n_mi-faq-page-qa.name",
      "settings": {
        "use_own_file": false,
        "modifier": "none",
        "updated_info": false,
        "heading": "<h2><strong>01. Sorry, you'll stop hoping your collagen cream worked overnight. </strong></h2>",
        "text": "<p>You bought it because the jar said collagen. Here's what the jar left off.</p><p>Your skin blocks almost anything larger than 500 Daltons. That's the real number dermatologists use… </p><p>A collagen molecule is about 300,000.</p><p>So it can't get in. Not \"slowly.\" Can't. It sits on top, feels nice for an hour, then rinses onto your pillow.*</p><p>Micro-Infusion goes beyond the barrier. The 24K gold-plated 0.5mm needles open thousands of tiny channels and deliver the serum underneath that protective layer to, where your skin can use it.</p><p><strong>Past the barrier, not onto it.</strong>*</p>"
      }
    },
